      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "About one minute. The goal is reliable\nmulti-step work, not just plausible text.\n\nThe crafting game gives a clear success\ncheck. The pickaxe is a simplified\nillustration.\n\nRLMs allow helper calls, but the recent\ncrafting tests isolate one model using\ntools. Do not claim a demonstrated benefit\nfrom recursion."
    },
    {
      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "RL is not a total failure. Answer-or-\nrefuse tests improved from 10 to 18\nsuccessful pairs out of 64, but extra\nsupervised training reached 19.\n\nPlanner training changed 53 to 56 correct\nout of 128; the gain was uncertain.\n\nSuccessful crafting attempts contained\nrejected actions. This motivates better\ncredit, but does not prove the cause."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "Teaching: 5 versus 15, then 3 versus 10\nsuccesses out of 32 in two training\nrepeats. Both teachers demonstrate\nlookups.\n\nCode assistance: 6 to 12, 8 to 10, 9 to\n14, and 9 to 13, each out of 16.\n\nCode uses already observed recipes, not\nhidden answers. Same game and related\ngoals; no broad transfer claim."
    },
